===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Away from the [[inside]] or [[centre]].
#: {{ux|en|The magician tapped the hat, and a rabbit jumped '''out'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|There was a hole in the bucket, and all the water leaked '''out'''.}}
# Away from, or at a [[distance]] from, some point of reference or focus.
#: {{ux|en|Once they had landed, the commandos quickly spread '''out''' along the beach.}}
#: {{ux|en|For six hours the tide flows '''out''', then for six hours it flows in.}}
#: {{ux|en|He lives '''out''' in Australia.}}
#: {{ux|en|It's three miles '''out''' to the island.}}
#: {{ux|en|The Joneses don't live here any more. They moved '''out''' three months ago.}}
## Specifically, [[away]] from [[home]] or one's usual place.
##: {{ux|en|Let’s eat '''out''' tonight}}
## Away from the doer, especially vigorously.
##: {{ux|en|hit '''out''', lash '''out''', speak '''out''', shout '''out''', yell '''out'''}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} Away, or at a distance, in time (relative to, and usually before, a stated event, or into the future) {{q|often preceded by a stated time period and followed by "from" or "to"}}
#: {{ux|en|Five weeks '''out''' from the passage of the law, something has to change.}}
#: {{ux|en|The election is a long way '''out'''.|q=a long way in the future}}
#: {{ux|en|Work may shift '''out''' as much as two weeks.}}
# Outside; not [[indoors]].
#: {{ux|en|Last night we slept '''out''' under the stars.}}
#: {{ux|en|It's cold '''out'''.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} Of the ball or other playing implement, so as to pass or be situated beyond the bounds of the playing area.
#: {{ux|en|The football caught the edge of the line but then bounced '''out'''.}}
# Into a state of non-operation or non-existence.
#: {{ux|en|Turn the lights '''out'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Put the fire '''out'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I painted '''out''' that nasty mark on the wall.}}
# To the end; completely; so that nothing remains.
#: {{ux|en|I haven’t finished. Hear me '''out'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Sorry love, we've got no bananas. We've sold '''out'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[write out|write '''out''']]}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|4|23|passage=Deceitful men shall not live '''out''' half their days.}}
#* '''1984''', "All cried out", song by English singer-songwriter Alison Moyet:
#*: I'm all cried '''out''' / You took a whole lot of loving for a handful of nothing
## {{n-g|Shows that an activity has been completed to the point of exhaustion.}}
##: {{ux|en|After hours at the party, she was all danced '''out'''.}}
# {{non-gloss|Used to [[intensify]] or [[emphasize]].}}
#: {{ux|en|The place was all decked '''out''' for the holidays.}}
# Into a state of existence or visibility.
#: {{ux|en|The singer is bringing '''out''' a new album next month.}}
#: {{ux|en|The sun has brought the flowers '''out'''.}}
## {{lb|en|of the sun, moon, stars, etc.}} So as to be visible in the sky, and not covered by clouds, fog, etc.
##: {{ux|en|The sun came '''out''' after the rain, and we saw a rainbow.}}
# {{lb|en|cricket|baseball|of a player}} So as to be [[disqualified]] from playing further by some action of a member of the opposing team (such as being [[stump|stumped]] in cricket or a [[force out|forced out]] in baseball).
#: {{ux|en|Wilson was bowled '''out''' for five runs.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1876|title=The School newspaper Vol. [2 issues of vols. 31 and 32].|author=|page=66|passage=First ball hit me on the 'and, second 'ad me on the knee, the third was in my eye, the fourth bowled me '''out'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1984|title=Official Baseball Guide|author=|page=211|passage=Hayes batted for Reed and grounded '''out''', Murray unassisted.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|title=Third Strike: A Brady Coyne/J. W. Jackson Mystery|author=Philip R. Craig; William G. Tapply|page=27|passage=So, first guy, Larry strikes him '''out''', good fastball in on his hands.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|title=Learn to Play Cricket: Teach Yourself|author=Mark Butcher; Paul Abraham|page=A-65|passage=The striking batter is bowled '''out''' when the wicket is broken with the bowler's delivery. A batter is bowled '''out''' whether or not the ball is touched or deflected into the stumps by the batter.}}

